# An allow-list: nothing in the repository reaches a build context but
# the directories a Dockerfile copies from. The
# exclusions below it came one leak at a time -- data/raw tarred into
# every build, a conflict copy of a Java class, a spec edit rebuilding
# the bundle -- and every new top-level folder was in every context
# until someone noticed: .claude/worktrees (whole copies of the repo),
# data/labels (the owner's ratings), .env (the keys),
# infra/local-https/certs (the phone's certificate key), apps/ios/, apps/android/.
# None of them is read by a Dockerfile; now none of them is sent.
*
!engine/
!services/planner/
!services/ingest/
!services/weather/
!services/gateway/
!services/jobs/
!apps/web/
!ml/requirements-*.txt
!infra/dev-services/

# Inside those: what no Dockerfile reads.
services/planner/tests/
services/planner/tests_wingtip/
services/ingest/tests/
services/weather/tests/
services/jobs/*/tests/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/node_modules/
**/target/
# ~600MB (FAA NASR/DOF, OSM, elevation/magnetic-variation caches) -- not
# needed at build time (services mount the project dir at runtime), but was
# being tarred into the build context on every `docker compose build` for
# any service using `context: .`. Found 2026-09-08 after repeated
# unexplained build hangs on this Intel Mac's Docker VM.
data/raw/
# Same reasoning as data/raw/ above -- generated/large, not needed at
# build time, and was still being tarred into the build context for
# every service using `context: .` (gateway, ml, the planner...).
data/processed/
data/models/
# Build output/dependency dirs for the two toolchains built *inside*
# their own Dockerfile stages: a local `npm install`/`mvn package` run
# outside Docker (e.g. for editor tooling, tests) leaves these on disk,
# and without this they'd get copied into the build context on every
# `context: .` build even though the Dockerfile never reads them (it
# does its own npm ci/mvn package from source instead).
apps/web/node_modules/
services/gateway/target/
# Tool caches and a local venv from running things outside Docker --
# host-only, never read by any Dockerfile (every image installs its own
# dependencies from a requirements.txt/package.json), small on their own
# (.venv is ~21M) but still worth keeping out of a context that already
# has a documented history of surprising leaks (see data/raw/ above).
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
apps/web/test-results/
# The browser suite, its reports and a host build of the bundle: none
# read by services/gateway/Dockerfile, and an edited spec used to
# invalidate `COPY apps/web/` and rebuild the bundle for nothing.
apps/web/e2e/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/dist/
# The gateway's own tests: the image is built with -DskipTests, and a
# test edit used to rebuild the jar for nothing.
services/gateway/src/test/
# iCloud's numbered conflict copies ("UnverifiedEmailException 2.java"),
# which .gitignore already hides from git but which still reached the
# build context: a copy of a Java class compiled as a duplicate and
# broke the gateway image on 2026-09-24. Never wanted in an image.
**/* [0-9].*
engine/target/
